12.235 emacsvox-url-template
============================

It is often useful to have "parametrized hot list entries" i.e., hotlist
entries that are "templates" for the actual URL. The user provides
values for the parametrized portions of the URL e.g.  the date.  See
*Note URL Templates::, for details on the URL templates that are
presently defined.

12.235.1 Emacsvox-Url-Template Commands
---------------------------------------

12.235.1.1 emacsvox-url-template-fetch
......................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-url-template-fetch (&optional documentation)
     ‘C-e u’

     Fetch a pre-defined resource.
     Use Emacs completion to obtain a list of available resources.
     Resources typically prompt for the relevant information
     before completing the request.
     Optional interactive prefix arg displays documentation for specified resource.

     (fn &optional DOCUMENTATION)

12.235.1.2 emacsvox-url-template-help
.....................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-url-template-help

     Display documentation for a URL template.
     Use Emacs completion to obtain a list of available
     resources.

12.235.1.3 emacsvox-url-template-load
.....................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-url-template-load (file)

     Load URL template resources from specified location.

     (fn FILE)

12.235.1.4 emacsvox-url-template-nls-add-to-wishlist
....................................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-url-template-nls-add-to-wishlist (book)

     Add book under point to wishlist.

     (fn BOOK)

12.235.1.5 emacsvox-url-template-save
.....................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-url-template-save (file)

     Save url templates.

     (fn FILE)

12.235.2 emacsvox-url-template Options
--------------------------------------

 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-stock-tickers
     Set this to the stock tickers you want to check. Default is
     the current fab-7!. Tickers is a list of stock symbols sorted in lexical order
     with duplicates removed when saving as a list of string.

     Default Value:

     ("aapl" "amzn" "goog" "meta" "msft" "nflx" "nvda")



