12.241 emacsvox-we
==================

we is for webedit Invoke XSLT to edit/transform Web pages before they
get rendered.  we makes emacsvox's webedit layer independent of a given
Emacs web browser EWW This module will use the abstraction provided by
browse-url to handle Web pages.

12.241.1 Emacsvox-We Commands
-----------------------------

12.241.1.1 emacsvox-we-class-follow-and-filter
..............................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-we-class-follow-and-filter (class url &optional
          prompt)
     ‘C-e x e y’

     Follow url and point, and filter the result by specified class.
     Class can be set locally for a buffer, and overridden with an
     interactive prefix arg. If there is a known rewrite url rule, that is
     used as well.

     (fn CLASS URL &optional PROMPT)

12.241.1.2 emacsvox-we-class-follow-and-filter-link
...................................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-we-class-follow-and-filter-link (&optional prompt)
     ‘C-e x e v’

     Follow url and point, and filter the result by specified class.
     Class can be set locally for a buffer, and overridden with an
     interactive prefix arg. If there is a known rewrite url rule, that is
     used as well.

     (fn &optional PROMPT)

12.241.1.3 emacsvox-we-count-matches
....................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-we-count-matches (url locator)
     ‘C-e x e C-f’

     Count matches for locator  in Web page.

     (fn URL LOCATOR)

12.241.1.4 emacsvox-we-count-nested-tables
..........................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-we-count-nested-tables (url)
